    "core_finding": "Direct empirical test of measured mechanical work in Joules predicting post-exercise MVIC torque on held-out human participants confirms that adding mechanical work does not statistically significantly improve prediction over baseline models (95% CI covers zero in all sensitivity analyses). On this dataset, incremental predictive value of mechanical work is not established beyond baseline force and condition indicators.",
    "architecture_a_implication": "Architecture A direct module coupling between scalar mechanical work and residual muscular force capacity is not supported by the available open human resistance datasets: endurance cycling power (Jutlah, ~18 kJ), resistance leg press volume (Norbury et al. 2024, 4-5 tonne-reps), and ankle plantarflexion EQI work (Križaj, ~140 J). The scientific status of Architecture A remains CONDITIONAL_POTENTIAL_WHOLE_SYSTEM_HOLD."
